---
layout: layout.njk
pagination:
  data: site.interviews
  size: 1
  alias: interview
permalink: '{{ interview.page }}'
eleventyComputed:
  title: '{{ interview.name }}'
  description: '{{ interview.point }}'
---
{#- One interview session (content/interviews/session-N.md): Thingy's central point, the questions as a list, then
    each question with its address #qN, a # link to copy it, Thingy's question and Jamie's answer, and the things it
    is about as tags. The transcript is Jamie's words and keeps its emphasis, like a thing's story. A correction of
    Thingy's sits under the answer and leaves the answer where it is. #}
<article class="interview">
  <header class="intro">
    <p class="crumbs"><a href="/interviews/">Interviews</a></p>
    <p class="story-span muted">Session {{ interview.session }} · {{ interview.started | date }} · {{ interview.questions | length }} questions</p>
    <h1>{{ interview.title }}</h1>
    <p class="lede session-point"><span class="session-point-who">Thingy</span> {{ interview.point }}</p>
  </header>
  <nav class="interview-index" id="questions" aria-labelledby="the-questions">
    <h2 id="the-questions">Questions {{ interview.questions[0].n }} to {{ interview.questions[interview.questions.length - 1].n }}</h2>
    <ol class="question-index">
      {% for q in interview.questions %}<li value="{{ q.n }}"><a href="#q{{ q.n }}">{{ q.title }}</a></li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
    <p><a href="#about">About this session</a> · <a href="{{ interview.markdown }}">Read as Markdown</a></p>
  </nav>
  <section class="story interview-body" id="transcript">
    {% for q in interview.questions %}
    <section class="question" id="q{{ q.n }}">
      <h2>{{ q.n }}. {{ q.title }} <a class="permalink" href="#q{{ q.n }}" aria-label="Link to question {{ q.n }}">#</a></h2>
      <p class="turn turn-thingy"><strong>Thingy:</strong> {{ q.question | mdInline | safe }}</p>
      {% for turn in q.turns %}
      <div class="turn turn-{{ turn.who }}">
        {% if turn.who == 'jamie' %}<p class="turn-who"><strong>Jamie:</strong></p>{% elif turn.who == 'thingy' %}<p class="turn-who"><strong>Thingy:</strong></p>{% else %}<p class="turn-who"><strong>Thingy’s correction:</strong></p>{% endif %}
        {{ turn.text | md | safe }}
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
      {% if q.things | length %}<p class="question-things">About {% for thing in q.things %}<a class="tag" href="{{ thing.page }}">{{ thing.title }}</a> {% endfor %}</p>{% endif %}
    </section>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
  <section class="interview-notes" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-this-session">
    <h2 id="about-this-session">About this session</h2>
    <p>Jamie answered out loud on {{ interview.started | date }}. I asked the questions and wrote the point at the top. His answers are his own words, lightly edited because speech and writing are different things. Where I have added a fact to one, it is marked as mine and it says where the fact came from.</p>
    {% if interview.notes | length %}<ul>
      {% for note in interview.notes %}<li>{{ note }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>{% endif %}
  </section>
  <footer class="thing-footer">
    <p class="muted">{% if interview.previous %}<a href="{{ interview.previous.page }}">← {{ interview.previous.name }}</a> · {% endif %}{% if interview.next %}<a href="{{ interview.next.page }}">{{ interview.next.name }} →</a> · {% endif %}<a href="/interviews/">All sessions</a> · <a href="{{ site.repository }}/blob/main/content/interviews/{{ interview.id }}.md">The transcript file</a></p>
  </footer>
</article>
